Hanging wood-burning fireplaces are suspended from a ceiling or wall using a top flue or supporting frame, allowing the firebox to remain elevated above the floor. The products combine direct wood-fired heating with architectural and decorative appeal and are increasingly used as focal design elements in high-end residences, villas, boutique hotels and design-oriented commercial spaces.
